.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.TH AUDIAKI 1 "2026-08-04" "audiaki 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
audiaki \- record an ALSA capture device to a WAV file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B audiaki
[\fIOPTION\fR]... \fIOUTPUT.WAV\fR
.br
.B audiaki
\fB\-\-probe\fR [\fB\-D\fR \fIDEVICE\fR]
.br
.B audiaki
\fB\-\-list\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B audiaki
opens an ALSA capture device, negotiates the widest sample format the hardware
supports, and streams the audio into a canonical PCM WAV file while drawing a
live peak meter on standard error.
.PP
The WAV header is written with placeholder sizes and patched when recording
stops, including when it is stopped with
.BR SIGINT " or " SIGTERM ,
so interrupted recordings are still valid files.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-device " " \fINAME\fR
ALSA device to capture from. Defaults to the value of
.B AUDIAKI_DEVICE
or, when that is unset,
.BR default .
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-rate " " \fIHZ\fR
Sample rate in Hz (default 44100). If the device cannot provide it, the nearest
supported rate is used and a warning is printed.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-channels " " \fIN\fR
Channel count (default 2).
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " " \fINAME\fR
Force a capture format:
.BR s16_le ", " s24_3le ", " s24_le " or " s32_le .
By default the best format the device offers is chosen, preferring
.B s32_le
then
.BR s24_3le ", " s24_le " and " s16_le .
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-duration " " \fISPEC\fR
Stop after the given time, written as
.IR SS ", " MM:SS " or " HH:MM:SS .
Fractional seconds are accepted. Recording stops on an exact frame count.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-period " " \fIFRAMES\fR
Period size in frames (default 1024). Larger values are more robust against
overruns at the cost of latency in the meter display.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-periods " " \fIN\fR
Periods per buffer (default 4).
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-force
Overwrite the output file if it already exists. Without this flag an existing
file is an error.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-meter
Do not draw the peak meter. The meter is suppressed automatically when standard
error is not a terminal.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Report errors only, and disable the meter.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Also report device negotiation details.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
List capture-capable PCM devices on standard output and exit.
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-probe
Print the formats, channel counts, rates and buffer sizes the device supports,
then exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH METER
.PP
.nf
 00:12 [##################|          ]  \-8.4 dBFS  xruns:0
.fi
.PP
The bar spans \-60 dBFS to 0 dBFS. The
.B |
marker holds the highest peak seen so far.
.B CLIP
appears once a sample reaches full scale.
.B xruns
counts buffer overruns; a rising count means the machine could not keep up with
the device.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AUDIAKI_DEVICE
Default ALSA device, used when
.B \-D
is not given.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Recording completed, or the requested information was printed.
.TP
.B 1
The device could not be opened or configured, or the file could not be written.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was malformed.
.SH EXAMPLES
Record until interrupted:
.PP
.nf
.RS
audiaki take01.wav
.RE
.fi
.PP
Record 90 seconds from a specific device at 48 kHz:
.PP
.nf
.RS
audiaki \-D plughw:CARD=Box,DEV=0 \-r 48000 \-t 1:30 take02.wav
.RE
.fi
.SH NOTES
Little-endian hosts only. Output is plain 44-byte-header PCM WAV, so a
recording stops at the 4 GB RIFF size limit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR arecord (1),
.BR alsamixer (1)
.SH BUGS
Report issues at https://github.com/HilthonTT/audiaki/issues
